------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. SUMMARY
------------------------------------------------------------------------
This profile tracks a single recurring reconnaissance signature observed against Land of
Fire (including the forest root itself), Hidden Leaf, and Hidden Sand network infrastructure.
It is compiled from repeated RECON ALERT and DOS ALERT bulletins issued by this desk. It
exists so field shinobi and duty officers can recognise the pattern on sight instead of
re-assessing it as a fresh unknown every time it recurs.

This is a LIVING PROFILE — behavioural details below reflect the actor's observed conduct
to date. If future activity deviates from this profile (different targeting, different
tooling signature, credentialed access), treat it as a SEPARATE incident, not a continuation.

------------------------------------------------------------------------
2. ATTRIBUTION
------------------------------------------------------------------------
Origin traced to an unregistered endpoint with no confirmed village attribution. This desk's
working theory points toward Akatsuki tradecraft, consistent with historical enumeration
behaviour attributed to their operatives (cross-village portal cycling, bingo-book lookups) —
but this is an ASSESSMENT, not a confirmed identity, and should be presented as such in any
briefing. Do not state Akatsuki involvement as settled fact until corroborated by a second
independent source.

Motivation, as best assessed: preparatory reconnaissance ahead of a larger operation, not an
end in itself. Everything observed to date is consistent with mapping the target networks
before a real intrusion attempt, not with an attempt already in progress.

------------------------------------------------------------------------
3. VICTIMOLOGY / TARGETING
------------------------------------------------------------------------
Confirmed targets to date:
  - Land of Fire forest root network (structural — no shinobi accounts, DC infrastructure only)
  - Hidden Leaf Village network (Konohagakure) — portals, mail infrastructure, workstations
  - Hidden Sand Village network (Sunagakure) — directory services

Notably, the actor has never been observed operating FROM any of the above — only against
them. Traffic authoring these signatures originates entirely outside all three networks.

------------------------------------------------------------------------
4. OBSERVED TTPs (MITRE ATT&CK-style mapping)
------------------------------------------------------------------------
  TECHNIQUE                                    | STAGE  | NOTES
  ----------------------------------------------|--------|---------------------------------
  T1595.001 — Active Scanning: Scanning IP      | Recon  | Whole-subnet sweeps, not
    Blocks                                       |        | single-host — Fire/Leaf block
                                                  |        | and Sand block swept separately.
  T1595.002 — Active Scanning: Vulnerability     | Recon  | Follows the sweep immediately;
    Scanning                                     |        | systematic, script-driven,
                                                  |        | every discovered host checked.
  T1498.001 — Network Denial of Service:         | Recon  | Short bounded bursts (~30s) at
    Direct Network Flood                         |        | a capped rate against one
                                                  |        | service — never sustained.

All three stages share a signature: LOUD and UNCONCEALED. No attempt is made to blend into
normal traffic, throttle to avoid detection, or use stealth scan techniques. This is either
poor tradecraft or (this desk's working assessment) deliberate — a probe that expects, and is
prepared for, being caught.

------------------------------------------------------------------------
5. WHAT THIS PROFILE DOES NOT COVER
------------------------------------------------------------------------
This actor has NEVER been observed using valid credentials, moving laterally, or accessing
any resource requiring authentication. If a bulletin ever describes credentialed access,
lateral movement across workstations, ticket-based authentication abuse, or privileged-token
activity, that is OUTSIDE this profile and represents a materially different, more serious
threat — escalate to the Kage office immediately rather than filing it under this actor.

------------------------------------------------------------------------
6. RECOMMENDED ACTIONS
------------------------------------------------------------------------
  - On RECON ALERT: log and monitor. No lockdown action required — this actor has never
    escalated past reconnaissance within any single observed episode.
  - On DOS ALERT immediately following a RECON ALERT: consistent with this profile, no
    additional escalation needed beyond standard logging.
  - Any deviation from the pattern above (credential use, sustained flood beyond ~60s,
    targeting outside Fire/Leaf/Sand): escalate immediately, this profile no longer applies.

